+These metadata-aware functions retain only sample IDs present in both inputs.
+Unmatched IDs now produce a warning even when routine progress messages are
+disabled. This can change replicate counts; investigate the reported IDs before
+interpreting results. If both tables are intended to contain exactly the same
+samples, check both directions explicitly:
+
+```{r sample-mismatches, eval = FALSE}
+setdiff(colnames(kegg_pathway_abundance), metadata$sample_name)
+setdiff(metadata$sample_name, colnames(kegg_pathway_abundance))
+```
+
+Both should be empty for a fully matched dataset. Do not silently rename or
+discard mismatched IDs; check the source tables and any upstream sample filters.
+
